  {
   "id": "I-001",
   "severity": "Informational",
   "evidence_level": "reasoning_only",
   "title": "Floating compiler pragma and UNLICENSED identifier on the token source file",
   "component": "WallitelliToken",
   "location": {
    "path": "contracts/WallitelliToken.sol",
    "start": 1,
    "end": 2
   },
   "category": "Best practice",
   "category_key": "evm.best_practice",
   "description": [
    {
     "p": "The token file declares a caret pragma range instead of the exact compiler version {fact:compiler.version} used for the verified deployment, and marks the source as UNLICENSED. The deployed bytecode is already fixed, so the pragma affects only future rebuilds and verification; the license identifier affects how third parties may reuse the source."
    }
   ],
   "impact": [
    {
     "p": "A later rebuild with a newer compiler in the allowed range could produce different bytecode and complicate re-verification. The UNLICENSED marker restricts reuse of a file that is otherwise a thin wrapper over an MIT-licensed library."
    }
   ],
   "recommendation": [
    {
     "ul": [
      "Pin the pragma to the exact version used for deployment.",
      "Choose an explicit license identifier such as MIT if the source is meant to be public."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "evidence": {
    "code": [
     {
      "code": {
       "ref": {
        "path": "contracts/WallitelliToken.sol",
        "start": 1,
        "end": 2
       },
